# Domain Model & Workflows

Preserve Design Document terminology exactly.

## Roles & Permissions

| Role | Prototype permissions |
| --- | --- |
| **Student** | View all room statuses |
| **CR** | View all + update **assigned** classroom(s) only |
| **Society Rep** | View all + update **assigned** Activity Space(s) only |
| **Teacher** | View all + assign/revoke CRs + optional status override |
| **Admin/DOA** | Full access: rooms, users, assignments, status overrides |

CR/Society access is **assignment-based**, not global update rights.

**Auth (prototype only):** no real auth — user/role selector stored in `st.session_state`.

## Tables

- `users` — id, name, email, role, created_at (`student` \| `cr` \| `teacher` \| `admin` \| `society_rep`)
- `rooms` — id, name, building, floor, room_type, created_at
- `room_assignments` — id, user_id, room_id, assignment_role, assigned_by, active, created_at (deactivate, do not hard-delete)
- `status_logs` — id, room_id, status, note, updated_by, created_at (append-only; current status = latest log per room)

## Statuses

- **Classroom:** Teacher not arrived · Class ongoing · Cancelled · Changed · Free
- **Activity Space:** Occupied · Open to all (optional note, e.g. society name)

`room_type` controls which statuses are valid.

## Core Loop to Preserve

**Assign → Update → Persist → View → Track History**

1. Teacher assigns Student as CR for a room → `room_assignments`
2. CR updates status → new `status_logs` row
3. Student sees status + history on Dashboard
4. Teacher revokes assignment → CR can no longer update that room

## UI Navigation (Prototype)

Dashboard · My Updates (CR/Society) · Teacher Panel · Admin Panel — rooms grouped by building/floor with status, note, last updated, recent history.
